# Code owners for the Envo / Stockroom repo.
# Lines below the catch-all are more specific and take precedence.
# See https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositories-settings-and-customizations/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Why this exists: Ryder (junior dev, frontend visual changes only) has Write
# access to push branches and open PRs, but branch protection on `main`
# requires review from CODEOWNERS for the paths listed below. Anything
# touching those paths needs StoveGodCooks's approval before merge.

# Default owner for everything not matched below.
*                           @StoveGodCooks

# Backend / database — authoritative on schema, RLS, RPCs.
/db/**                      @StoveGodCooks

# Infrastructure / build / deploy config.
/wrangler.jsonc             @StoveGodCooks
/vite.config.js             @StoveGodCooks
/package.json               @StoveGodCooks
/package-lock.json          @StoveGodCooks
/.github/**                 @StoveGodCooks

# Core libs — the Supabase client, auth flow, and data layer are sensitive.
/src/lib/supabase.js        @StoveGodCooks
/src/lib/auth.jsx           @StoveGodCooks
/src/lib/items.js           @StoveGodCooks

# Top-level docs that describe scope or process.
/BRIEF.md                   @StoveGodCooks
/README.md                  @StoveGodCooks

# Frontend visual layer is intentionally NOT pinned to an owner here, so PRs
# from Ryder that only touch components/pages/styles don't require backend
# review. Branch protection still requires *some* approval — that's the
# floor, but specifically the CODEOWNERS gate only fires on the paths above.
